From 1693c62d581870be197cf9937cabdabbb7043ada Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:03:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] agentHost: keep tool attribution across a steering preempt

A steering message is injected with priority 'now', which makes the SDK
emit a result envelope for the preempted turn even though the protocol
turn is still running. The mapper cleared the tool_use attribution map
and drained foreground subagent spawns on every result envelope, so a
tool call still in flight when the steer landed lost its attribution:
its later tool_result hit the unknown tool_use_id path, no
ChatToolCallComplete was emitted, and the tool stayed Running forever.
A foreground subagent spawn vanished the same way, so subagent_started
was never announced and its inner signals stayed buffered.

The pipeline already decides whether a result is final (queue drained)
or intermediate, and already defers ChatTurnComplete to that decision.
This moves the turn-end cleanup to the same place rather than passing
the decision into the mapper: mapResult no longer touches the mapper
state or the registry, and the pipeline calls the router's new
clearPendingTurnState on the final result only, just before it fires
ChatTurnComplete. The router is the natural owner since it already
holds both the mapper state and the registry reference, and the mapper
no longer performs turn-end cleanup it cannot time correctly.

Abort and dispose paths did not rely on the per-result clear: the
consumer loop stops routing once the controller is aborted, and any
stale entries are still dropped on the next final result with the
existing orphan warnings. The registry's own dispose still clears
everything.
